Discussion and Future Works
We propose a novel GAN-based architecture, Conditional TremorGANs, designed to generate tremor sensor data for healthy individuals, PD patients, and DD patients. To our knowledge, this is the first model specifically designed to generate Parkinsonian tremor data collected from smartwatches. We enhance the standard conditional GANs framework by integrating a temporal encoding module and a temporal self-attention mechanism into the generator. At the same time, the discriminator is equipped with a timefrequency enhancement module and a multi-scale feature extraction module. The input data for the proposed model are sourced from the PADS dataset, which contains recordings from participants performing three distinct task categories. To better capture task-specific tremor characteristics, we design three separate neural network branches within Conditional TremorGANs, each tailored to one task category, thereby improving the representativeness and diversity of the generated sensor data.
